            <ArticleTitle>A case of multiple spontaneous coronary artery dissections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>318-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissections are relatively uncommon. Many of the previously reported cases have involved a dissection in a single coronary artery of a peripartum or postpartum female. We describe an unusual case of multiple spontaneous coronary dissections in a middle-aged male.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
